<title>UK: Sullom Voe berthings suspended due to high winds.</title>
<headline>Sullom Voe berthings suspended due to high winds.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Berthing at the Sullom Voe Brent Blend crude oil terminal in the Shetland Islands was suspended at midnight on Sunday due to strong winds, a port official said on Monday.</p>
<p>He said one tanker was scheduled to arrive at 1400 local time on Monday but noted the outlook was for continuing high winds.</p>
<p>Three tankers successfully loaded and sailed on Sunday several hours before the suspension, the official said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7646</p>
